{
 "esm": "2.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cism_diva_discretization",
  "description": "Local EarthSciDiscretizations-format discretization rules for the CISM DIVA depth-integrated momentum balance on the 2-D vertex grid (stage 2 of the EqESM project; CISM = cismwrap_3_00_002 / cism_main_3.00.002 as built in CESM cesm3.0-alphabranch, glissade_velo_higher.F90 compute_element_matrix for which_ho_approx = HO_APPROX_DIVA = 4, F90:8171-8181, on the gris20 20 km grid of the reference run). The DIVA x-momentum balance D(2*etaH*(2*D(u,x)+D(v,y)),x) + D(etaH*(D(u,y)+D(v,x)),y) - beta_eff*u = rhoi*g*H*D(s,x) (Goldberg 2011 eq. 37 with the depth-integrated membrane viscosity etaH = H*int(efvs dsigma), the vertical average of the effective viscosity times the thickness, the h_qp*efvs_qp_vertavg coefficient the Fortran assembles at each quadrature point, F90:5400-5407) expands to four second-derivative terms: D(4*etaH*D(u,x),x) (the Kuu = 4*phi_x*phi_x + phi_y*phi_y block, F90:8178), D(2*etaH*D(v,y),x) (the Kuv = 2*phi_x*phi_y + phi_y*phi_x block, F90:8179), D(etaH*D(u,y),y) (the phi_y*phi_y part of Kuu) and D(etaH*D(v,x),y) (the phi_y*phi_x part of Kuv); the y-momentum balance is the mirror set. The rules lower each term to a staggered, conservative face-flux divergence at the vertices with the cell-centered coefficient etaH: the face of vertex (i,j) in the +x direction passes through the cell centers (i+1,j) and (i+1,j+1) (the east face of the vertex, midpoint of the east cell edge), so its flux coefficient is the mean k_E = (etaH(i+1,j) + etaH(i+1,j+1))/2, and likewise k_W = (etaH(i,j) + etaH(i,j+1))/2 for the west face, k_N = (etaH(i,j+1) + etaH(i+1,j+1))/2 for the north face and k_S = (etaH(i,j) + etaH(i+1,j))/2 for the south face; the flux difference is divided by dx^2 (or dy^2) for the repeated derivatives. The mixed terms D(k*D(psi,y),x) and D(k*D(psi,x),y) use the same face coefficients with the 4-point face-centered stencils of the inner derivative: D(psi,y) on the east face is (psi(i,j+1) + psi(i+1,j+1) - psi(i,j-1) - psi(i+1,j-1))/(4*dy) and on the west face (psi(i-1,j+1) + psi(i,j+1) - psi(i-1,j-1) - psi(i,j-1))/(4*dy), so the two mixed terms reduce to the standard centered DxDy = (psi(i+1,j+1) - psi(i+1,j-1) - psi(i-1,j+1) + psi(i-1,j-1))/(4*dx*dy) stencil when the coefficient is constant (probed: the Dx_Dy and Dy_Dx rules reduce exactly to that stencil for constant k). The rules are marked ESD PR candidates: the EarthSciDiscretizations library (${ESD_ROOT}) has no staggered variable-coefficient second-derivative rules on a vertex grid (its cartesian_uniform_2d rules cover cell-centered first/second derivatives of the C-grid dynamics, and cice_bgrid the B-grid stress integrals), so this file carries the four rules locally until they are reviewed upstream. Grid contract: the rules match D(k*D(psi,..),..) trees with psi a 2-D vertex field of THIS grid (shape [i,j] on the i/j index sets) and k ANY expression (probed: a where clause on the compound coefficient breaks the match, so the rules constrain only psi); the free names dx/dy (the grid spacings) and the metaparameters NX/NY (the vertex-grid dims) come from the consuming model. The etaH depth integral is lowered by the fifth rule: cism_sigma_integral_field matches integral(f, var: lev, lower: z_sfc, upper: z_top) with f a [lev,i,j] field and lowers it to the per-cell composite midpoint sum sum_l f[l,i,j]*dz[l] over the consumer's free-name layer measure dz (the sigma layer widths, cism_sigma_measure of ./cism_velo_discretization.esm), the exact vertical-average sum of F90:5366-5369. The ESD column_nonuniform_1d integral rules cannot lower this node (their where clause requires a [lev]-shaped integrand), which is why the field form lives here.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "esd:rule",
   "family:finite_volume",
   "grid:cism_vertex",
   "op:derivative",
   "op:integral",
   "axes:i,j",
   "order:2",
   "stencil_width:1",
   "bc:none",
   "spec:9.6.8"
  ],
  "created": "2026-11-06T00:00:00Z",
  "authors": [
   "EqESM project contributors"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "CISM (Community Ice Sheet Model) cismwrap_3_00_002 / cism_main_3.00.002, as built in CESM cesm3.0-alphabranch (checkout stage1/cesm/components/cism, reference run T1850Gg/f09_g17_gris20): libglissade/glissade_basal_traction.F90, libglissade/glissade_therm.F90, libglissade/glissade_grid_operators.F90, libglissade/glissade_velo_higher.F90, libglissade/glissade_mass_balance.F90, libglissade/glissade_calving.F90, libglissade/glissade_masks.F90, libglissade/glissade_utils.F90, libglimmer/glimmer_physcon.F90, libglimmer/glimmer_utils.F90, libglide/glide_types.F90, libglide/glide_setup.F90, libglad/glad_main.F90, libglad/glad_timestep.F90, libglad/glad_output_states.F90, libglad/glad_output_fluxes.F90, drivers/cpl/nuopc/glc_import_export.F90 - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
    "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CESM"
   },
   {
    "citation": "CISM (Community Ice Sheet Model) cism_main_3.00.002, libglissade/glissade_velo_higher.F90 compute_element_matrix (F90:8171-8181) and the assembly loop (F90:5336-5407)."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Goldberg, D. N. (2011). A variationally derived, depth-integrated approximation for a full-Stokes ice sheet model. Journal of Glaciology, 57(204), 717-728. Eq. 37 (the depth-integrated momentum balance) and eq. 40-41 (the effective basal friction)."
   },
   {
    "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.13 (nonuniform grids and conservative flux forms)."
   },
   {
    "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
    "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NX": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 9,
   "description": "Number of vertices along x of the 2-D vertex grid (the patch: dump_patch_n + 1 = 9 for the reference run)."
  },
  "NY": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 9,
   "description": "Number of vertices along y of the 2-D vertex grid (dump_patch_n + 1 = 9)."
  },
  "NLAYERS": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 10,
   "description": "Number of CISM sigma layers (upn - 1 = 10 for the reference run); the DIVA velocity levels number NLAYERS + 1 (k = 1 surface .. k = NLAYERS+1 bed: the CISM sigma interfaces, the dump's sigma_001..011)."
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "i": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NX"
  },
  "j": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NY"
  }
 },
 "expression_templates": {
  "cism_stag_Dx_Dx": {
   "description": "Staggered x-x second derivative with a cell-centered variable coefficient at the vertices: lowers D(k*D(psi,x),x) to the conservative face-flux difference (k_E*(psi(i+1,j) - psi(i,j)) - k_W*(psi(i,j) - psi(i-1,j)))/dx^2, with the east-face coefficient k_E = (k(i+1,j) + k(i+1,j+1))/2 and the west-face coefficient k_W = (k(i,j) + k(i,j+1))/2 - the two cell centers the face of vertex (i,j) passes between. The DIVA x-momentum term D(4*etaH*D(u,x),x) applies it with psi = u and k = 4*etaH. Interior vertices only (i,j in 2..NX-2, 2..NY-2, matching the guard `i <= NX-2 and j <= NY-2` in the rule body): the stencil needs the neighbor vertices and the east/west face cells, so it is not evaluated on the patch boundary. ESD PR candidate: no staggered variable-coefficient rule of this form exists in EarthSciDiscretizations.",
   "params": [
    "psi",
    "k"
   ],
   "priority": 10,
   "match": {
    "op": "D",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "k",
       {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
         "psi"
        ],
        "wrt": "x"
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "wrt": "x"
   },
   "where": {
    "psi": {
     "shape": [
      "i",
      "j"
     ]
    }
   },
   "body": {
    "op": "faq",
    "output_idx": [
     "i",
     "j"
    ],
    "args": [
     "psi",
     "k"
    ],
    "ranges": {
     "i": [
      1,
      "NX"
     ],
     "j": [
      1,
      "NY"
     ]
    },
    "expr": {
     "op": "ifelse",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": "and",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": ">=",
         "args": [
          "i",
          2
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "i",
          {
           "op": "-",
           "args": [
            "NX",
            2
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": ">=",
         "args": [
          "j",
          2
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "j",
          {
           "op": "-",
           "args": [
            "NY",
            2
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "op": "/",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "-",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "*",
             "args": [
              0.5,
              {
               "op": "+",
               "args": [
                {
                 "op": "index",
                 "args": [
                  "k",
                  {
                   "op": "+",
                   "args": [
                    "i",
                    1
                   ]
                  },
                  "j"
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "op": "index",
                 "args": [
                  "k",
                  {
                   "op": "+",
                   "args": [
                    "i",
                    1
                   ]
                  },
                  {
                   "op": "+",
                   "args": [
                    "j",
                    1
                   ]
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "op": "-",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                "psi",
                {
                 "op": "+",
                 "args": [
                  "i",
                  1
                 ]
                },
                "j"
               ]
              },
              {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                "psi",
                "i",
                "j"
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "*",
             "args": [
              0.5,
              {
               "op": "+",
               "args": [
                {
                 "op": "index",
                 "args": [
                  "k",
                  "i",
                  "j"
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "op": "index",
                 "args": [
                  "k",
                  "i",
                  {
                   "op": "+",
                   "args": [
                    "j",
                    1
                   ]
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "op": "-",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                "psi",
                "i",
                "j"
               ]
              },
              {
               "op": "index",
               "args": [
                "psi",
                {
                 "op": "-",
                 "args": [
                  "i",
                  1
                 ]
                },
                "j"
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          "dx",
          "dx"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      0.0
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "cism_stag_Dy_Dy": {
   "description": "Staggered y-y second derivative with a cell-centered variable coefficient at the vertices: lowers D(k*D(psi,y),y) to the conservative face-flux difference (k_N*(psi(i,j+1) - psi(i,j)) - k_S*(psi(i,j) - psi(i,j-1)))/dy^2, with the north-face coefficient k_N = (k(i,j+1) + k(i+1,j+1))/2 and the south-face coefficient k_S = (k(i,j) + k(i+1,j))/2. The DIVA x-momentum term D(etaH*D(u,y),y) applies it with psi = u and k = etaH (and the y-momentum term D(4*etaH*D(v,y),y) with psi = v, k = 4*etaH). Interior vertices only. ESD PR candidate (see cism_stag_Dx_Dx).",
