  "cism_sigma_integral_field": {
   "description": "Whole-column sigma integral of a [lev,i,j] field at the cell centers: lowers integral(f, var: lev, lower: z_sfc, upper: z_top) with f a layer field of the 2-D vertex grid to the per-cell composite midpoint sum sum_l f[l,i,j]*dz[l] over the consumer's free-name layer measure dz (the dimensionless sigma layer widths dsigma[l] = sigma[l+1] - sigma[l], cism_sigma_measure of ./cism_velo_discretization.esm). This is the exact stencil of the Fortran vertical average of the effective viscosity at each quadrature point, efvs_qp_vertavg = sum_k efvs_qp(k,p)*(sigma(k+1) - sigma(k)) (glissade_velo_higher.F90:5366-5369, applied per cell to the quad-point-mean layer viscosities by the stage-2 DIVA model); the physical column integral carries the thickness factor in the model (etaH = thck*integral(efvs, ...)), not in the measure, matching the omega integrals of ./cism_velo_discretization.esm. The ESD column_nonuniform_1d integral rules cannot lower this node (their where clause requires a [lev]-shaped integrand; the ESD integral rules and the free-name bounds contract are otherwise identical - z_sfc/z_top and the dz measure), so the field form lives here. Implementation notes (probed): the per-cell reduce faq materializes its output over the halo and reads the const-array integrand at the ghost cells, so the body carries the explicit 1-based ranges on ALL axes (i, j and the reduce axis l, the ESD NLEV-style binding convention) and the in-range guard on i/j (a guarded read is not performed, esm-spec 5.5.5; the ghost cells then take the 0 of the guard's false branch, exactly the zero-ghost value the stencil needs). The reduce axis is spelled as the explicit range [1, NLAYERS], NOT the `from` index-set form (probed: the `from` form adds a spurious term in the per-cell reduce). ESD PR candidate: a [lev, i, j] whole-column integral rule for the cartesian grids.",
   "params": [
    "f",
    "dz"
   ],
   "priority": 10,
   "match": {
    "op": "integral",
    "args": [
     "f"
    ],
    "var": "lev",
    "lower": "z_sfc",
    "upper": "z_top"
   },
   "where": {
    "f": {
     "shape": [
      "lev",
      "i",
      "j"
     ]
    }
   },
   "body": {
    "op": "faq",
    "output_idx": [
     "i",
     "j"
    ],
    "reduce": "+",
    "args": [
     "f",
     "dz"
    ],
    "ranges": {
     "i": [
      1,
      "NX"
     ],
     "j": [
      1,
      "NY"
     ],
     "l": [
      1,
      "NLAYERS"
     ]
    },
    "expr": {
     "op": "ifelse",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": "and",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": ">=",
         "args": [
          "i",
          1
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "i",
          "NX"
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": ">=",
         "args": [
          "j",
          1
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "<=",
         "args": [
          "j",
          "NY"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "f",
          "l",
          "i",
          "j"
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "dz",
          "l"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      0.0
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "cism_stag_vertex_gradient_x": {
   "description": "CISM plain vertex gradient of a cell-centered field in x (glissade_grid_operators.F90 glissade_gradient with gradient_margin = 1, F90:309-468, as called by glissade_slope_angle_staggered F90:1414-1552): lowers cism_stag_vertex_gradient_x(f) to df_dx(i,j) = 0.5*((f(i+1,j+1) - f(i,j+1)) + (f(i+1,j) - f(i,j)))/dx - the average of the two east-west edge gradients bracketing vertex (i,j) (the NE-corner convention: cell (i,j) has its NE corner at vertex (i,j); the edge north of the vertex runs between cells (i,j+1) and (i+1,j+1), the edge south between (i,j) and (i+1,j)). With the slope_mask = 1 default of the DIVA call site (no slope_mask_in argument, glissade_velo_higher.F90:2174-2193) the masked branch reduces to the plain average. The stage-2 DIVA model applies it to z_mean = 0.5*(usrf + lsrf) = usrf - thck/2 for the grounded patch cells; the DivaGeometry pointwise law of cism_velo.esm is the same stencil on the 4-cell parameters. Interior vertices only. ESD PR candidate (no staggered vertex-gradient rule exists in EarthSciDiscretizations).",
